cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Clarity in your research, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Clarity: a chat client for exact, replayable prompting experiments with local LLMs"
authors:
  - family-names: Samandari
    given-names: Andalib
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0004-9786-5285"
repository-code: "https://github.com/andalibmalit/clarity-chat"
license: Apache-2.0
version: 0.2.3
date-released: 2026-11-14
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.24068236
identifiers:
  - type: doi
    value: 10.5281/zenodo.24068236
    description: "All versions (concept DOI)"
  - type: doi
    value: 10.5281/zenodo.24068237
    description: "Version 0.1.0"
abstract: >-
  Clarity builds the token IDs for each call itself, sends every sampling value
  explicitly, checks that the backend used them, logs every setting and
  environment fact known to affect the output, and can replay any completed call.
  It runs local models through llama.cpp or Hugging Face Transformers.
keywords:
  - large language models
  - reproducibility
  - llama.cpp
  - transformers
  - prompting
